# 99-pci-runtime-pm.rules — let every PCI device use runtime power management.
#
# Install: sudo install -m644 misc/99-pci-runtime-pm.rules /etc/udev/rules.d/
# Applies at next boot, or immediately with:
#   sudo udevadm control --reload && sudo udevadm trigger --subsystem-match=pci
#
# Nine PCI devices on this machine ship with power/control=on, i.e. runtime PM
# disabled outright: the NPU, GNA, Dynamic Tuning, CNVi WiFi, NVMe, shared
# SRAM, eSPI and SPI. Flipping them to auto let HD Audio, SMBus, eSPI and a
# Realtek device actually reach suspended. It matters beyond their individual
# draw -- any single device pinned in D0 can keep the whole package out of
# PC8/PC10, which is where the multi-watt idle savings are.
#
# This is the PCI half of what `powertop --auto-tune` does, and deliberately
# NOT the rest of it. Auto-tune also enables USB autosuspend across the board,
# which is the usual cause of a laggy mouse or a keyboard that drops the first
# keypress after idle. Restricting the rule to the PCI subsystem keeps the
# win without that class of breakage.
#
# To undo: rm /etc/udev/rules.d/99-pci-runtime-pm.rules
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="pci", ATTR{power/control}="auto"
